  "entry": "code/README.md",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Pick named star groups (the solar neighbourhood, open clusters, globular clusters), pull their Gaia DR3 photometry with a live query, and plot colour index against absolute magnitude on a Hertzsprung–Russell diagram you can zoom, pan, colour by theme and export as a poster. Data used in the run: public. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
